TITLE:: FxRack
summary:: chains of effects side by side inside a chain, lined up in time
categories:: Libraries>ParaEQ
related:: Classes/FxChain, Classes/FxUnit, Classes/FxRackBranch, Classes/Compressor

DESCRIPTION::
An effect whose inside is several chains in parallel. What comes in goes to
every chain, what comes out of them is added up. It is an link::Classes/FxUnit::,
so it goes in an link::Classes/FxChain::, is switched on and off, and is saved
with the chain like any other effect.

code::
(
r = FxChain.master.add(FxRack());        // one chain to begin with: nothing changes
r.branches[0].name = "squash";
r.branches[0].chain.add(Compressor()).enabled = true;
b = r.addBranch("dry");                  // a second chain, empty: the dry sound
b.level = -6;
r.enabled = true;
);
::

An empty chain passes the sound, so every chain that is added adds that much
level until something is put in it or its level is taken down.

subsection:: Latency

An effect that cannot help being late - a compressor's lookahead, a limiter, an
fft - says by how much with link::Classes/FxUnit#-latency::. The rack adds up what
is on in each chain and holds every other chain back by the difference, so what
is added up is in time and a dry chain beside a late one does not comb. Delays
are whole samples.

When a latency changes the rack waits link::#*settle:: seconds for it to stand
still, then crossfades to the new delays over link::#*crossfade:: seconds.

A rack lines up only what is declared: an effect that is late and answers 0
stays out of line.

subsection:: On the server

Where an effect has a synth a rack has a group. In it, in order: a copy of the
bus onto each chain's own bus, then each chain's group followed by that chain's
delay and level onto a sum, then the sum back onto the bus, faded in and out
like any effect. Switched off, the group is freed. The rack owns the buses and
gives them back when it is freed or leaves its chain. After cmd-period or a
reboot the chain it is in builds it again.

Each chain's delay line is link::#*delayFrames:: frames a channel, taken from the
server's real time memory.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
A rack with one empty chain, called "a". Add it to a chain to use it.

METHOD:: crossfade
Seconds a change of delay takes. Default 0.03.

METHOD:: settle
Seconds a latency has to stand still before the delays follow. Default 0.25.

METHOD:: delayFrames
The length of each channel's delay line: 32768 frames, 0.68 s at 48 kHz. A chain
that would have to wait longer stays out of line, and the rack says so once.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: branches
The chains, an Array of link::Classes/FxRackBranch::.

METHOD:: addBranch
Another chain beside the others, empty.

ARGUMENT:: name
What it is called; the next free letter when nil.

RETURNS:: the link::Classes/FxRackBranch::.

METHOD:: removeBranch
Takes a chain out, with its effects. The last chain stays.

ARGUMENT:: which
A branch, or its index.

METHOD:: branchAt
ARGUMENT:: which
An index, or a name.

RETURNS:: the link::Classes/FxRackBranch::, or nil.

METHOD:: numBranches
How many chains.

METHOD:: latency
How late the rack is, in seconds: its latest chain that is lined up. A chain
with code::align:: off does not count. The rack says code::changed(\latency)::
when it changes, so a rack in a chain of another rack is lined up too.

METHOD:: live
Set true and no chain is held back: nothing is added to the latency, and the
chains are out of line by whatever each one costs.

METHOD:: shown
The index of the chain a strip shows the effects of. Saved with the rack.

METHOD:: depth
0 in a chain of its own, 1 in a chain of another rack. A rack does not go deeper:
link::Classes/FxChain#-add:: answers nil and says why.

METHOD:: anySolo
Whether a chain is soloed.

METHOD:: settings
What a preset holds: code::live::, code::shown::, and for every chain its name,
level, mute, solo, align and effects. Setting it makes the rack exactly those
chains.

EXAMPLES::

A compressor in parallel with the dry sound, in time:

code::
(
c = FxChain(\bus16, 16, 2);
r = c.add(FxRack());
r.branches[0].chain.add(Compressor()).enabled = true;
r.branches[0].chain.units[0].lookahead = 0.01;
r.addBranch("dry");
r.enabled = true;
);
r.branches[1].heldBack;   // 0.01: the dry chain waits for the compressor
r.latency;                // 0.01
r.live = true;            // nothing held back
r.gui;
c.free;
::
